<?xml version="1.0"?>

<namelist_defaults>

<!--
Values used by default when creating the EOCN namelist.  Entries may be keyed
on `emulator` (EOCN_EMULATOR) or on `ocn_grid` (OCN_GRID); an unkeyed entry is
the fallback.
-->

<do_eocn>.true.</do_eocn>

<!-- SCRIP description of the eocn grid, relative to DIN_LOC_ROOT -->
<filename_eocn ocn_grid="gauss180x360">share/meshes/gaussian_180x360_latlon.scrip.20260127.nc</filename_eocn>

<eocn_model_device>gpu</eocn_model_device>
<eocn_rng_seed>0</eocn_rng_seed>
<eocn_interp_state>.true.</eocn_interp_state>
<eocn_flux_ifrac_unweight>.true.</eocn_flux_ifrac_unweight>
<eocn_unweight_stress>.false.</eocn_unweight_stress>
<eocn_precip_units>kg/m2/s</eocn_precip_units>

<!--
Where the ocean's ten forcing channels come from.

  atm_raw  the atmosphere emulator's own generated channels, published in this
           executable (shr_emul_flux_mod).  This is what reference SamudrACE
           does, and the two checkpoints name the channels identically, so
           they are used as they stand.  Falls back to `coupler`, once and
           with a log line, if no emulator atmosphere is publishing, which
           is the case for every EAM and EAMxx compset here.

  coupler  the fields the MCT driver merged.  The turbulent fluxes are
           recomputed from bulk formulae rather than the emulator's, every
           channel arrives weighted to the open-water share, and the
           shortwave has to be split into up and down with an assumed ocean
           albedo.  The only option with a non-emulator atmosphere.
-->
<eocn_forcing_source>atm_raw</eocn_forcing_source>

<!--
The masked trace is the default, and the one to use.  It applies fme's input
mask inside the graph, replacing every masked cell of every input channel with
that channel's training mean.  This matters most for the state channels, which
the emulator carries forward over land as well as ocean: fed back unmasked they
are a physical value the network has no representation for, and VERIFICATION.md
records what that produced: a 440 K sea surface.  `samudra_ocn_traced_cuda.pt`
is the same network without the mask, kept only for measuring what the mask is
worth.

Traced TorchScript model and matching initial condition.  Absolute paths
outside DIN_LOC_ROOT because neither the checkpoint nor its traced form is
distributed with E3SM inputdata yet; override in user_nl_eocn.
Produce them with tools/trace_eocn_model.py and tools/make_eocn_ic.py.
-->
<eocn_model_file emulator="SamudrACE-E3SMv3"
  >/pscratch/sd/m/mahf708/SamudrACE-E3SMv3/eocn/samudra_ocn_traced_masked_cuda.pt</eocn_model_file>
<eocn_ic_file emulator="SamudrACE-E3SMv3"
  >/pscratch/sd/m/mahf708/SamudrACE-E3SMv3/eocn/samudra_ocn_ic_0_icemask.nc</eocn_ic_file>

</namelist_defaults>
